\subsection{Logical Correctness Under Controlled Schedule Violations}
Due to the practical constraints of enforcing actual non-compliance for testing, we conducted a staged simulation.
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Setup:} A mock schedule assigned "Student A" to "Room 101" at 10:00 AM.
    \item \textbf{Action:} "Student A" entered the "Canteen Zone" (Zone 4) at 10:05 AM.
    \item \textbf{Result:} The system instantly detected the identity, queried the database, and flagged the schedule conflict.
\end{itemize}
These results validate logical correctness and system responsiveness rather than population-level behavioral inference.

Figure 2 demonstrates the system's output during this simulation. The Bounding Box overlay indicates a confirmed logic deviation.

% --- FIGURE 2: TRUANCY OVERLAY ---
\begin{figure}[H]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=0.95\columnwidth]{truancy_overlay.png}
\caption{Illustrative debugging overlay showing spatiotemporal mismatch between observed location and scheduled zone. Overlays are used solely for system validation and are not part of the deployed interface.}
\label{fig:overlay}
\end{figure}

\subsection{Speed and Latency Analysis}
Real-time performance is a non-negotiable requirement. We decomposed the processing latency per frame to ensure it fits within the 33ms budget of a 30 FPS stream.

\begin{table}[H]
\caption{Latency Decomposition per Frame}
\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{lcc}
\toprule
\textbf{Pipeline Stage} & \textbf{Time (ms)} & \textbf{Status} \\
\midrule
Identity Resolution (Upstream, External)\textsuperscript{*} & 18 ms & External \\
Schedule Lookup (CSV I/O) & 4 ms & I/O Bound \\
Logic Check (CSP) & $<1$ ms & CPU Bound \\
\textbf{Total Latency} & \textbf{$\approx$ 23 ms} & \textbf{Real-Time} \\
\bottomrule
\multicolumn{3}{l}{\textsuperscript{*}\footnotesize Identity resolution performed by upstream biometric module} \\
\multicolumn{3}{l}{\footnotesize (Paper 1) using upstream identity resolution. Schedule lookup latency measured on CSV} \\
\multicolumn{3}{l}{\footnotesize repository; PostgreSQL optimization is proposed future work. This paper's} \\
\multicolumn{3}{l}{\footnotesize core contribution is the CSP constraint evaluation logic (<1ms). All reported} \\
\multicolumn{3}{l}{\footnotesize latency values are measured using the CSV-based reference repository;} \\
\multicolumn{3}{l}{\footnotesize PostgreSQL performance is projected based on indexed schema design.}
\end{tabular}
\end{center}
\end{table}

